      "content": "The Horizon Build waterfront proposal faces significant geological risks, particularly regarding soil liquefaction and potential embankment failures during heavy storms, which are not easily \"worked around\" without prohibitively expensive and disruptive mitigation measures. These structural vulnerabilities align with the core concerns of the \"Stop the Piling\" coalition, as they pose a direct threat to the long-term stability and safety of the planned revitalization platform. While urban planning can integrate plinths or foundation modifications to mitigate these issues, the current trajectory of the city council and the scale of required go-arounds suggest the project may never gain the necessary regulatory approval to proceed.",
