      "content": "look, i'm not saying skip the safety stuff, but the council is basically breathing down my neck to find a path to \"yes.\" if we were to present a modified version where the developer commits to a higher-spec foundation plan—even if it hits their margins—would you still classify the liquefaction risk as a \"dealbreaker\" for the city, or is there a way to frame this as a manageable technical challenge rather than a reason to scrap the whole revitalisation?",
